p.src:
Large companies have manufacturing, R&D, sales, marketing, distribution, money, experience, brands, market knowledge, and customer relationships. Marina says they have nearly everything except the ability to pivot quickly. The startup edge is not that incumbents are stupid. The edge is maneuverability: $\text{startup edge}
=
\text{ability to pivot under incomplete information}.$ This matters because innovative markets do not present themselves as clean problem sets. We are not given all the variables. We are making decisions in fog. The startup must try, learn, and redirect.

