p.src:
The evidence hierarchy is: $\begin{aligned}
\text{compliment}
&< \text{reaction to idea} \\
&< \text{reaction to prototype} \\
&< \text{near-real product use} \\
&< \text{customer money}.\end{aligned}$ The closer the customer is to using the product as intended, the more useful the feedback becomes. Payment, deposits, and R&D contracts are the strongest signals in the lecture.

