p.src:
Fundraising itself is work. Research investors before pitching them. If an investor funds only AI software and the company is selling 3D printers, do not pitch and call it optimism. Marina’s rule is to reject yourself before collecting needless rejection. Every failed pitch should produce a strategic takeaway: $\text{failed pitch}
\longrightarrow
\{\text{wrong investor},\ \text{unclear pitch},\ \text{flawed business model}\}.$ Even rejection can be useful if it teaches whether the list, the communication, or the business model is wrong.

